{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"FunctionalGraphs","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cycleDecomposition"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","text":"FunctionalGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","text":"CycleDecomposition"}],"externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18cycleDecompositionAC05CycleE0VyF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"CycleDecomposition.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/CycleDecomposition.swift#L346"},"modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}],"title":"cycleDecomposition()"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The cycles of the graph, and every vertex’s tail, root and preimages. O(n) time, with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation per vertex. The result holds 5n + 3 "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s (two "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arrays for the preimage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows, one for the vertices by depth, a 12-byte record per vertex and a 4-byte preorder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number beside each vertex by depth), plus one per cycle and one per unit of the longest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tail; building it takes 3n more for a moment (two 12-byte entries per vertex)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A counting sort of f gives the preimage rows and the in-degrees. Peeling the vertices of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-degree zero, repeatedly, visits the tree vertices leaves first, summing subtree sizes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the way, and leaves exactly the cyclic ones; each cycle is then walked from its least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex. Revisiting the peeled vertices in reverse, parents first, gives every tail length"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and root and a preorder numbering of the trees from the subtree sizes; a counting sort by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depth then lays out the level-ancestor table. Nothing recurses or chases a chain of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependent reads, so a tail of 10⁷ vertices needs no call stack."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph has fewer than 2³¹ vertices.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[